---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"
import DocSection from "../../components/DocSection.astro"

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "me@maxlibin.com"
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "24 September 2026"
---

<Base
  title="ZhouYi Master AI — Terms of Use"
  description="The agreement that governs your use of the ZhouYi Master AI iOS app: the Yi Master subscription, acceptable use, liability."
  pathname="/zhouyi-master-ai/terms/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "ZhouYi Master AI", item: "/zhouyi-master-ai/" },
    { name: "Terms of Use", item: "/zhouyi-master-ai/terms/" },
  ]}
>
  <article class="mt-8 mb-16 px-4 md:px-0 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="mb-3 text-sm">
      <a href="/zhouyi-master-ai/" class="text-fg hover:underline">
        ← ZhouYi Master AI
      </a>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-fg mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint mb-10">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <DocSection title="Agreement">
      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") are an agreement between you and Max Li
        Bin, an independent developer based in Singapore ("we", "us"), governing
        your use of the ZhouYi Master AI iOS app ("the app"). Your use of the
        app is also governed by Apple's{" "}
        <a
          href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-fg hover:underline"
        >
          Licensed Application End User License Agreement
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        By downloading, installing, or using the app you agree to these Terms
        and to our{" "}
        <a href="/zhouyi-master-ai/privacy/" class="text-fg hover:underline">
          Privacy Policy
        </a>
        . If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Who can use the app">
      <p>
        You must be at least 13 years old to use the app. If you are under 18,
        you may only use it with the involvement of a parent or guardian who
        agrees to these Terms on your behalf.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="What the app does">
      <p>
        ZhouYi Master AI lets you cast coins, read hexagrams from the Book of
        Changes (Yijing, I Ching), and reflect on them with Yi Master, an AI
        guide. Yi Master's replies are generated by a large language model. They
        are offered for reflection and can be wrong, incomplete, or unsuitable
        for your situation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app does not predict the future and is not medical, psychological,
        legal, financial, or crisis advice. If you are in danger or crisis,
        contact your local emergency services.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="ZhouYi Master AI Monthly subscription">
      <p>
        Casting coins, reading the hexagrams, and your journal are free. Every
        installation also starts with free Yi Master replies. After those, Yi
        Master needs the ZhouYi Master AI Monthly subscription, an auto-renewing
        subscription sold and managed by Apple via the App Store.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>
          Each month includes about 3,700 typical Yi Master replies. Longer
          conversations and attached readings use more of the allowance.
        </li>
        <li>
          Unused replies do not carry over. If the allowance runs out, replies
          pause until the next renewal.
        </li>
        <li>
          Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          The subscription automatically renews each month unless auto-renew is
          turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          The renewal charge is taken within 24 hours before the period ends.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can manage and cancel your subscription in Settings → your name →
          Subscriptions on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          Refunds (if any) are handled by Apple under the App Store's standard
          refund policy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Acceptable use">
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>
          Send content that is illegal, infringes someone else's rights, or
          contains personal information about another person without their
          permission.
        </li>
        <li>
          Attempt to reverse-engineer, scrape, or otherwise abuse the app or our
          backend, or use it in a way that disrupts the service for other users.
        </li>
        <li>Use the app to develop a competing product.</li>
      </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Your content">
      <p>
        You keep all rights to the messages, readings, and profile details you
        write. You grant us a limited, worldwide, royalty-free license to
        process that content for the sole purpose of operating the app, which
        means generating Yi Master's replies.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Intellectual property">
      <p>
        The app, its design, artwork, branding, and code are owned by Max Li Bin
        and are protected by intellectual-property laws. We grant you a
        personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the
        app on Apple devices you own or control, in accordance with these Terms
        and Apple's standard EULA for App Store apps.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Disclaimers">
      <p>
        The app is provided "as is" and "as available". To the maximum extent
        permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied,
        including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
        non-infringement. AI-generated replies may be wrong; you are responsible
        for the decisions you make.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Limitation of liability">
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for any
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages
        arising out of or relating to your use of the app. Our total liability
        for any claim arising out of or relating to these Terms is limited to
        the amount you paid us (via Apple) in the 12 months before the claim
        arose, or, if you have not paid us anything, USD 50.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Termination">
      <p>
        You can stop using the app at any time by deleting it. We may suspend or
        terminate your access to Yi Master if you breach these Terms or if
        continuing the service becomes commercially or legally impractical.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Changes to these Terms">
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. We'll change the effective
        date above and, for material changes, surface a notice in the app.
        Continuing to use the app after a change means you accept the updated
        Terms.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Governing law">
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of Singapore, without regard to its
        conflict-of-laws rules. The courts of Singapore have exclusive
        jurisdiction over any dispute arising from these Terms, except where
        your local consumer-protection laws require otherwise.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Apple-specific terms">
      <p>
        You acknowledge that these Terms are between you and us, not Apple, and
        that Apple is not responsible for the app or its content. To the extent
        these Terms are inconsistent with Apple's standard EULA for App Store
        apps, the terms more protective of you apply. Apple and its subsidiaries
        are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them
        against you.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Contact">
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms?{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
      </p>
    </DocSection>
  </article>
</Base>
